# This file is vendored. Do not edit it.

`model/` and `training/base-model/` are upstream export packages from
[`owensong/Inflect-Micro-v2`](https://huggingface.co/owensong/Inflect-Micro-v2),
not our code. They ship their own weights, phoneme frontend and VITS runtime.

- **`model/checksums.sha256` verifies 24 files in that directory.** Any edit
  breaks verification, and the check is part of the release process.
- `.gitattributes` marks `model/**` as `linguist-vendored` so it stays out of
  our language statistics and collapsed in diffs.
- `training/base-model/` is not tracked at all — it is a 38 MB snapshot fetched
  by `python training/scripts/download_model.py`. Editing it edits a download.

## The characters here are IPA, not Azerbaijani

`model/runtime/text/symbols.py` and the phoneme code contain `ə`, `ɣ`, `ʃ`, `ɫ`
and friends. These are IPA phoneme symbols. A search for Azerbaijani letters
matches them. Do not translate, transliterate or normalise anything here.

## If the model needs to behave differently

Wrap it. `aztts/engine.py` exists precisely for this: it loads the package,
then adds Azerbaijani normalisation (`az_text.py`), chunking (`az_chunk.py`) and
optional restressing (`az_prosody.py`) around it. Every gap between "what the
upstream package does" and "what Azerbaijani needs" is closed in `aztts/`.

Two upstream facts worth knowing before you try to patch anything:

- `model/config.json` declares `accepts_prephonemized_input: true`, so phonemes
  can come from any frontend — you do not have to go through eSpeak.
- The package splits text itself only after 280 characters, which is far too
  late for this model. `az_chunk.py` cuts at ~15 words instead.
